message: "If you use or adapt this resource, please cite it as below."
title: "Hidden Treasure in Your Pocket: An Interactive Guide to Critical Elements in Smartphones"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Peter
    family-names: Nockemann
    affiliation: "Queen's University Belfast, UK"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9864-9702"
abstract: >-
  An interactive educational resource about the critical and strategic
  elements inside a smartphone, for pupils aged 11-16 and general audiences.
  Visitors take apart a 3D phone and select one of its parts (display, camera,
  circuit board, speaker, battery, casing) to explore which elements it
  contains, what they do, where they come from, and whether they are on the
  EU, US and UK critical raw materials lists. Includes a periodic-table view,
  a real-time recycling game, a scored quiz with certificate and a guide for
  teachers.
keywords:
  - critical raw materials
  - smartphones
  - e-waste
  - recycling
  - chemistry education
  - science communication
  - educational game
